Subject: [PATCH 2/2] =?UTF-8?q?fix(gb):=20fetch=20full=20mod=20data=20via?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20apiv6=20=E2=80=94=20thumbnails=20+=20metadata=20now=20load?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Root cause: apiv4 /Mod/Index returns STUB records with only _sName + _aCategory.
The _aPreviewMedia, _aSubmitter, _aFiles, _tsDateAdded fields are all null/zero,
which is why thumbnails were blank, author showed 'Unknown', date showed
'Added 56 years ago' (epoch), and files showed '0 file(s)'.

Fix: switch to a 2-step fetch:
  1. Core API (api.gamebanana.com/Core/List/New) returns mod IDs as
     [['Mod', 12345], ...] — small payload, always works
  2. For each ID, fetch full data via apiv6 /Mod/{id}?_csvProperties=...
     apiv6 returns _aPreviewMedia, _aSubmitter, _aFiles, _tsDateAdded,
     _nViewCount, _nLikeCount, _nDownloadCount, _aRootCategory, etc.

Parallelize step 2 with SemaphoreSlim(4) — for perPage=20 that's ~5 batches
of 4 concurrent requests, total latency ~1-2 seconds.

Sort final results by _tsDateAdded descending (newest first) to match
the original Index endpoint's default sort order.

Validated with manual test: 3/3 mods fetched successfully with all fields
populated including thumbnail URLs.

The apiv6 csvProperties used are all valid (tested individually):
  _sName, _sProfileUrl, _aPreviewMedia, _sDescription, _aSubmitter,
  _aCategory, _aRootCategory, _aFiles, _tsDateAdded, _tsDateModified,
  _nViewCount, _nLikeCount, _nDownloadCount, _aAlternateFileSources
